  "response": "The pipeline has been fully assembled! Here's a summary of everything that was built:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfd4\ufe0f Heightfield Pipeline \u2014 Complete\n\n### Processors Added\n| Processor | Role |\n|---|---|\n| **HeightFieldMapper** | Converts the `Heightfield` image source to a normalized single-channel float image suitable for displacement |\n| **MeshCreator** (Plane, 128\u00d7128) | Generates a high-resolution plane mesh as the geometric base for the terrain |\n| **HeightFieldRenderGL** | The main renderer \u2014 displaces the mesh using the height data and shades with textures |\n| **Canvas** | Displays the final rendered heightfield |\n\n### Connections Made\n```\nHeightfield (ImageSource)\n    \u2514\u2500\u25ba HeightFieldMapper [image \u2192 image]\n            \u2514\u2500\u25ba HeightFieldRenderer [heightfield \u2192 heightfield]\n\nMeshCreator (Plane 128\u00d7128)\n    \u2514\u2500\u25ba HeightFieldRenderer [outport \u2192 geometry]\n\nColor (ImageSource)\n    \u2514\u2500\u25ba HeightFieldRenderer [image \u2192 texture]   \u2190 color texture\n\nNormalMap (ImageSource)\n    \u2514\u2500\u25ba HeightFieldRenderer [image \u2192 normalmap]  \u2190 normal map\n\nHeightFieldRenderer\n    \u2514\u2500\u25ba Canvas [image \u2192 inport]\n```\n\n### Tips\n- **Terrain Shading** property on `HeightFieldRenderGL` can be switched to *Color Texture* mode to use the `Color` image for surface coloring.\n- Increase the **Height Scale** property on the renderer to exaggerate the terrain elevation.\n- Adjust **Scaling Mode** on `HeightFieldMapper` (fixed range, custom range, or sea-level-based) to control how height values are mapped.",
